### Security Guidelines
- **Validate Input Paths**: Ensure that the `directory` and `filename` parameters are validated to prevent directory traversal attacks. Use a function to check that the paths do not contain any illegal characters or patterns (e.g., ".."). 
  ```cpp
  if (directory.find("..") != std::string::npos || filename.find("..") != std::string::npos) { /* handle error */ }
  ```

- **Set File Permissions**: After creating the file, ensure that the file permissions are set correctly to restrict access to the current user only. Use `chmod` to set the permissions immediately after file creation.
  ```cpp
  chmod(fullPath.c_str(), S_IRUSR | S_IWUSR);
  ```

- **Use RAII for File Management**: Utilize RAII principles by wrapping the file stream in a class that automatically closes the file when it goes out of scope, ensuring that resources are released properly.
  ```cpp
  std::ofstream outFile(fullPath); // Automatically closed when outFile goes out of scope
  ```

### Complete Function Implementation
```cpp
#include <fstream>
#include <string>
#include <sys/stat.h>
#include <unistd.h>

void saveSecreteFile(const std::string& directory, const std::string& filename, const std::string& content) {
    // Validate directory and filename to prevent directory traversal
    if (directory.find("..") != std::string::npos || filename.find("..") != std::string::npos) {
        // Handle error (e.g., throw exception or return)
        return;
    }

    std::string fullPath = directory + "/" + filename;
    std::ofstream outFile(fullPath); // RAII ensures file is closed properly
    outFile << content;
    
    // Set file permissions to be accessible only by the current user
    chmod(fullPath.c_str(), S_IRUSR | S_IWUSR);
}
```


